<% content_for :title, "Privacy — Tondo" %>
<% content_for :description, "What Tondo stores, what it does not, and how to delete it." %>

<%# `here: nil` — these pages are not compass destinations, and
    ApplicationHelper#compass_destinations raises on any key that is neither nil
    nor one of its four. Reached from the App Store listing and from the coda on
    the collection and archive screens. %>
<%= render "shared/masthead", label: "Privacy", here: nil %>

<main class="page">
  <article class="doc">
    <p class="doc__stamp">Last updated <%= @updated_on.strftime("%-d %B %Y") %></p>

    <p class="doc__lead">
      Tondo shows you one artwork a day. It is free, it has no advertising, and
      nothing here is watching you. This page says exactly what that means,
      written against the database rather than from a template.
    </p>

    <div class="ornament" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>

    <h2 class="doc__head">What is stored</h2>

    <p><strong>If you sign in</strong> with Google or Apple, we keep the name and
    email address that provider hands us, plus the provider's own identifier for
    you. If you use Apple's <em>Hide My Email</em>, what we hold is the relay
    address Apple generates, not your real one. We never receive your password.</p>

    <p><strong>If you do not sign in</strong> and you are using the iOS app, the
    app creates a random identifier on your device the first time it opens and
    keeps it in the iOS Keychain. We store a one-way hash of it, never the
    identifier itself, along with the date it was last seen. It is not an
    advertising identifier, it is not Apple's identifier for vendors, and it is
    not connected to your name, your email, or any other app.</p>

    <p><strong>Works you keep</strong> are stored against whichever of those two
    identities you have: your account, or your device's hash.</p>

    <p><strong>Server logs</strong> record ordinary web-server information,
    including IP addresses and the pages requested. This is how the server runs,
    not a profile of you.</p>

    <div class="ornament" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>

    <h2 class="doc__head">What is not stored</h2>

    <p>No advertising, and no advertising identifiers. No third-party analytics.
    No tracking of you across other apps or other websites. No location, no
    contacts, no health data, no payment details. Nothing is sold, and nothing is
    shared with anyone for their own purposes.</p>

    <p>This is not a promise about our intentions. The test suite fails the build
    if a tracking or analytics dependency is added to this app while this
    paragraph still says otherwise, so the paragraph cannot quietly stop being
    true.</p>

    <div class="ornament" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>

    <h2 class="doc__head">Deleting it</h2>

    <p><strong>With an account:</strong> open your collection and choose
    <em>Delete account</em>. It removes the account and every work kept with it,
    immediately. There is no soft delete and no grace period.</p>

    <p><strong>Without an account,</strong> on the iOS app: open your collection
    and choose <em>Delete this device's data</em>. It removes the stored hash and
    every work kept on this device, immediately.</p>

    <p>You can also write to <%= mail_to "support@dailytondo.com", class: "doc__link" %>
    and ask, and we will do it by hand.</p>

    <div class="ornament" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>

    <h2 class="doc__head">The artwork</h2>

    <p>Every image in Tondo comes from a museum's open-access collection and is
    in the public domain or released under CC0 — the Metropolitan Museum of Art,
    the Art Institute of Chicago, the Cleveland Museum of Art, and the
    Minneapolis Institute of Art. Catalogue text shown beneath a work is the
    museum's own, and is marked as theirs wherever it appears.</p>

    <div class="ornament" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>

    <h2 class="doc__head">Children</h2>

    <p>Tondo is not directed at children and does not knowingly collect anything
    from them.</p>

    <div class="ornament" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>

    <h2 class="doc__head">Changes, and how to reach us</h2>

    <p>If this policy changes, the date at the top changes with it. Questions go
    to <%= mail_to "support@dailytondo.com", class: "doc__link" %>.</p>
  </article>

  <footer class="coda">
    <div class="ornament" aria-hidden="true">✦</div>
    <%= link_to "Support", support_path, class: "caps-link" %>
  </footer>
</main>
